Structure of the database tables

We plan to use **PostgreSQL as one shared cloud database**. The table below are proposed designs, not claims that the database is already live.

### Table 1: `conversion_history` (for Conversion)

| Column | Data type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| history_id | BIGSERIAL | Primary key for a conversion |
| session_key | VARCHAR(64) | Keeps one browser session’s history together |
| original_input | VARCHAR(50) | Number or Roman numeral entered |
| conversion_type | VARCHAR(20) | Direction of the conversion |
| output_value | VARCHAR(50) | Calculated result |
| created_at | TIMESTAMPTZ | When the conversion happened |
